    {"description":"Generated values for protocol, renderer and smoke tests. It runs no SQL, so any connection id is accepted; a disconnect of that id still ends it.","hidden":"pause","id":"debug.synthetic","label":"Synthetic","probes":["debug.synthetic.metrics","debug.synthetic.table","debug.synthetic.status","debug.synthetic.grid","debug.synthetic.log","debug.synthetic.wide"],"scope":"none","testOnly":true},
    {"description":"SQL Server's own activity, read from server DMVs on the connection's \" - Activity Monitor\" pool (READ UNCOMMITTED, LOCK_TIMEOUT 1000, DEADLOCK_PRIORITY LOW). Its probes, tables, columns and series come from the Activity Monitor's catalogue (docs/activity-monitor.md). Each probe runs several statements (Activity/ActivitySql.cs), and one the login may not run fails alone, naming what it feeds. Args: one filter per table (Processes' view chip and toggles, the filter box, column value filters, Hide benign waits) and the Details flyout's session (focusSession).","hidden":"pause","id":"activity","label":"Activity Monitor","probes":["activity.overview","activity.sessions","activity.resources"],"scope":"server","testOnly":false}
